# Orquestrador — testes

Intent (“teste”, “spec”, “coverage”) já aciona `testing`. Esta rule **confirma** framework e contexto quando há arquivos de teste abertos ou no diff.

## JavaScript / TypeScript

| Detectar | Skills |
| --- | --- |
| Vitest, Jest, RTL, `*.test.ts(x)`, `*.spec.ts(x)` | `testing` |
| Teste de componente UI | `testing` + `accessibility` (axe, roles) |

Refs: `testing/references/vitest.md`, `react-testing-library.md`, `accessibility-testing.md` (dir. da skill resolvida)

## PHP

| Detectar | Skills |
| --- | --- |
| PHPUnit, Pest, `tests/` Laravel | `testing` + `laravel/references/testing.md` |
| Teste unitário PHP sem Laravel | `testing` (adaptar) + `php` |

## Composição

- `skills-orchestrator-react-ui.mdc` se teste em `.tsx`
- `skills-orchestrator-php-stack.mdc` se teste em `.php`
- `skills-orchestrator-base.mdc` (sempre)
